From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:11:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: an OpenCode refusal says what the vendor said, and
 for how long

lingengyuan (#5509): OpenCode Go 429'd Claude Code's /v1/messages with
the 5-hour window at 3%, and what magpie said of each refusal was its
status and the names of the headers sent - a short rate limit and a
spent allowance read alike, and the routing log row keeps no body of a
try that later succeeded. The refusal now says the wait the vendor
names (Retry-After, or a ratelimit reset header, said as how long from
now) and its own words - the body, or the message in it, clipped - with
the body put back for what reads it next, bare 400s included
(openCodeBareRefusal reads it after). The line is still one a refusal.

A 429 of this shape is a moment's trouble and the walk already treats
it so: passing() waits it out and the reporter's own turn went through
on the fourth try. What was missing was the saying, not the doing.

Run: TestOpenCodeRefusalSaysWhatTheVendorSaid, ...SaysABareBodyAndNoWait
and ...SaysADatedWaitAsHowLong - the first two red on main (the new
tests do not compile against the old signature), green here; go test
-tags nogui ./internal/gateway full package green; gofmt, vet (darwin,
GOOS=linux) and the build clean.
---
 internal/gateway/gateway.go                   |   2 +-
 internal/gateway/opencode_refusal_log_test.go | 118 ++++++++++++++++++
 internal/gateway/opencode_session.go          |  30 ++++-
 3 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 internal/gateway/opencode_refusal_log_test.go

